How about some actual math rather than an ad hominem argument? Given n
spellbooks collected by the player, the probability that Create
Familiar shows up at least once (in Vanilla) is  1 - (99/100)^n,
versus 1 - (98/100)^n for Charm Monster. For n small, Charm Monster
shows up around twice as often, but for large n, the difference isn't
as distinct. For instance, if a player encounters 20 spellbooks before
the Valley, then the probability of Charm Monster showing up is 33%,
versus 18% for Create Familiar. For thirty spellbooks, it's 26% versus
45%. And if some crazy polypiler reads 100 (morphed) books, it's 63%
versus 86%.

Even for 20 spellbooks, the difference is not that great. Derek is
right.



